# Generated run reports. The report directory is configurable; this is the
# default and is also excluded from snapshot manifests and cache identity.
#
# The second pattern is not redundant: the first has an inner slash, so git
# anchors it to the repository root, and the project artefacts are written into
# whatever workspace a run is pointed at. A test or a manual run against one of
# the corpus modules under fixtures/ produces `fixtures/<name>/reports/mutation`,
# which the anchored pattern does not cover and which must never be committed.
reports/mutation/
**/reports/mutation/

# Release artifacts, the locally built CLI, and compiled test binaries.
dist/
bin/
/go-mutants
*.test
*.exe

# Go toolchain and coverage scratch output.
*.out
*.prof

# Failing cases persisted by pgregory.net/rapid. These are development scratch,
# not a curated corpus: rapid replays every file it finds here on the next run,
# so committing one silently pins an arbitrary shrunk case and reports it as a
# stale failure once the code under test moves on. A seed worth keeping is
# promoted by hand to a named table case next to the property test instead.
# The leading **/ is load-bearing: a pattern with an inner slash would anchor to
# the repository root and miss every internal/<pkg>/testdata/rapid/.
**/testdata/rapid/

# Linter caches.
.rumdl_cache/
